I'm Bilikis, a Business Administration graduate who works at the point where business questions meet data.

My background gave me a practical understanding of how organisations run: how sales, costs, people and customers connect, and what managers actually need to know to make a decision. My final-year research, on how leadership shapes the performance of food businesses in Lagos, taught me to frame a clear question, gather evidence and explain what it means in plain language.

I bring that same approach to data. I don't stop at reporting what happened. I look for why it happened and what the business should do next, and I check every number against common sense before it reaches a decision-maker.

In August 2026 I attended Deep Learning Indaba 2026 at Pan-Atlantic University in Lagos, Africa's leading annual gathering of the machine learning and AI community. It showed me how quickly data and AI are changing the way African businesses make decisions, and how much room there is for analysts who understand both the business and the data.

I'm open to junior business intelligence and data analyst roles, internships and project work. If you're hiring, or you have a problem you think data could help with, I'd be glad to hear from you.
